```
Insertion at known position: O(1) amortized
Memory overhead: ~24 bytes per node (2 pointers + allocator metadata)
Cache behavior: TERRIBLE — each element is a separate heap allocation
Allocator calls: One malloc/free per insertion/deletion
```

### `std::vector`
```
Insertion at middle: O(n) due to memmove of all trailing elements
Memory overhead: Near-zero (contiguous storage)
Cache behavior: EXCELLENT — sequential memory access
Allocator calls: Rare (only on reallocation)
```

## Key Real-World Factors

| Factor | `std::list` | `std::vector` |
|---|---|---|
| Insert cost (after iterator) | ~10–50 ns | ~n × 1–3 ns (memmove) |
| Cache misses per insert | ~1–3 | ~0 (if data fits in L1/L2) |
| Memory fragmentation | High | Low |
| Traversal speed | Slow | Fast |
| Allocation overhead | Per-element | Amortized over bulk |

