|---|---|---|---|
| `sqrt + log` per iter (~100M iters) | ~850 ms | ~2,800 ms | **~3.3x** |

### 2. Array Processing / Map-Reduce Pattern
```go
// Go
results := make([]float64, n)
for i := 0; i < n; i++ {
    results[i] = math.Pow(data[i], 2.5)
}
total := 0.0
for _, v := range results {
    total += v
}
```
```javascript
// Node.js
const results = new Float64Array(n);
for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    results[i] = Math.pow(data[i], 2.5);
}
let total = 0;
for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    total += results[i];
}
```

| N = 10 million | Go | Node.js | Ratio |
|---|---|---|---|
| pow + reduce | ~420 ms | ~1,100 ms | **~2.6x** |

### 3. JSON Parsing Throughput (I/O-bound mixed with logic)
This is where the gap **narrows significantly**:

| Operation | Go (`encoding/json`) | Node.js (`JSON.parse`) | Ratio |
|---|---|---|---|
| Parse 1MB JSON doc | ~1.2 ms | ~0.

