# Node.js vs Go: Tight Loop Performance Comparison

## Benchmark Setup

Here's a concrete comparison using an identical algorithm in both languages. We'll measure a tight loop that performs integer arithmetic and array operations — a representative "heavy iteration" workload.

### The Algorithm (Same Logic in Both Languages)

A nested loop performing:
- Integer addition, multiplication, and modulo operations
- Array reads/writes
- Conditional branches

---

## Code Implementations

### Go (`main.go`)

```go
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"time"
)

func heavyLoop(iterations int) float64 {
	result := 0.0
	arr := make([]int, iterations)

	// Initialize array
	for i := 0; i < iterations; i++ {
		arr[i] = i * 3 + 1
	}

	start := time.Now()

	// Heavy computation loop
	sum := 0
	for i := 0; i < iterations; i++ {
		temp := arr[i]
		for j := 0; j < 10; j++ {
			temp = temp*7 + i
			temp = temp % 1000000
			sum += temp
			if temp%2 == 0 {
				sum -= 1
			}
		}
		result += float64(temp)
	}

	elapsed := time.Since(start)
	fmt.Printf("Go: Iterations=%d, Elapsed=%v\n", iterations, elapsed)
	return result
}

func main() {
	// Warm-up run
	heavyLoop(1_000_000)

	// Timed runs
	const warmups = 3
	const timedRuns = 5
	const iterations = 10_000_000

	for r := 0; r < warmups; r++ {
		heavyLoop(iterations)
	}

	var total time.Duration
	for r := 0; r < timedRuns; r++ {
		result := heavyLoop(iterations)
		_ = result
	}
	// Note: each call to heavyLoop prints its own elapsed time above
}
```

### Node.js (`index.js`)

```javascript
const iterations = 10_000_000;

function heavyLoop(iterations) {
    const arr = new Int32Array(iterations);

    // Initialize array
    for (let i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {
        arr[i] = i * 3 + 1;
    }

    const start = process.hrtime.bigint();

    // Heavy computation loop
    let sum = 0;
    let result = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {
        let temp = arr[i];
        for (let j = 0; j < 10; j++) {
            temp = temp * 7 + i;
            temp = temp % 1000000;
            sum += temp;
            if (temp % 2 === 0) {
                sum -= 1;
            }
        }
        result += temp;
    }

    const elapsed = Number(process.hrtime.bigint() - start) / 1e9; // seconds
    console.log(`Node.js: Iterations=${iterations}, Elapsed=${(elapsed * 1000).toFixed(2)}ms`);
    return result;
}

// Warm-up runs
for (let r = 0; r < 3; r++) {
    heavyLoop(iterations);
}

// Timed runs
for (let r = 0; r < 5; r++) {
    heavyLoop(iterations);
}
```

